#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0336 expect=violation domain=CV
#note "No label= and no class= anywhere: the rule reads neither, and inventing SEND labels would assert something with no authority behind it. CVDTC is type=Char, NEVER type=Date -- a Date column is parsed to a SAS numeric at load. The key tuple is (CVTESTCD, USUBJID, CVDTC, CVNOMDY, CVTPT, CVTPTNUM, CVSTINT, CVENINT, CVEVLINT); the four widened members are NOT DECLARED here, and GroupSemantics.uniqueSetViolations keeps only column indices >= 0, so they are dropped and the partition is the same one the pre-M3-D15 four-key form used. CVSEQ is not in the tuple, which is why rows 1 and 2 are duplicates despite distinct sequence numbers; `not is_unique_set` flags the first-seen row AND the repeat, so the count is 2. Row 3 differs in CVDTC -> silent. CVSTINT/CVENINT are blank on every row and FOLD_BLANK_KEYS keeps a blank as a real, equal component."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 CVTESTCD=HR
#expectViolationAt row=2 CVTESTCD=HR
dataset CV
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col CVSEQ    type=Num
col CVTESTCD type=Char
col CVDTC    type=Char
col CVSTINT  type=Char
col CVENINT  type=Char
---
S1 | CV | ANIMAL1 | 1 | HR | 2023-03-20 |  |
S1 | CV | ANIMAL1 | 2 | HR | 2023-03-20 |  |
S1 | CV | ANIMAL1 | 3 | HR | 2023-03-21 |  |
---
